<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hun Manet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1977</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hun Manet is a Cambodian army officer and politician, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a>, who became prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> in August 2023. A graduate of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Military Academy at West Point, he rose to command the Royal Cambodian Army before succeeding his father, who had led the government since 1985, after elections dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodian-peoples-party">Cambodian People's Party</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hun-manet.jpg" alt="Hun Manet" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cabinet Public Relations Office of the Cabinet Secretariat · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hun_Manet_on_May_30,_2025_(cropped_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
